# Feature for both runtimes

When the user wants something that works on **both** PWA and desktop (also: `/feature-both`, “shared feature”, “works on both”):

1. **Read:** [`docs/PWA_DESKTOP_COMPAT.md`](../../docs/PWA_DESKTOP_COMPAT.md)
2. **Follow:** `.cursor/skills/feature-both/SKILL.md`

## Required pattern

- Shared UI/engine in `js/` + `react/`
- Platform differences only via `js/platform` contracts + web and windows providers
- Optional native acceleration via capabilities — web must still work
- Done only after tests + web build + desktop build + dual smoke (or explicit desktop smoke list if Tauri unavailable here)

## Forbidden

- Implementing desktop-first then “porting” to PWA
- `@tauri-apps/*` outside `js/platform/windows/`
- Claiming done after browser-only verification when the request was dual-runtime
